.TH UHUB-SEEDER 1 "August 2026"
.\" Please adjust this date whenever revising the manpage.
.SH NAME
uhub\-seeder \- seed cache daemon for the uhub ADC hub
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uhub\-seeder
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
uhub\-seeder keeps content posted in hub chat available after the user who
posted it has left.
.PP
It is not part of the hub. It logs into a uhub as a registered bot account and
behaves as an ordinary ADC client: it appears in the user list, watches chat
for content\-addressed embeds, downloads the referenced file from the user who
posted it, verifies the file against its TTH and stores it in a local cache.
From then on it answers
.B TR
searches for that TTH and serves the file over ordinary client\-to\-client
connections, so the content stays reachable on a hub where every other user is
passive, and remains reachable after the poster disconnects.
.PP
Because it runs as a separate process it can fail without affecting the hub.
Nothing it does needs hub internals, and a crash, a stalled disk or a hostile
input costs the operator the seed cache and nothing else.
.PP
uhub\-seeder needs a listening port of its own and must be reachable from the
outside; a passive seeder cannot serve passive clients, which is the entire
point of running one. See
.B doc/seedcache.txt
for setup, the embed format, the wire exchange, operator commands and the
security considerations.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
.BI \^\-v
Verbose mode, add more \-v's for higher verbosity.
.TP
.BI \^\-q
Quiet mode, if quiet mode is enabled no output or logs are made.
.TP
.BI \^\-f
Fork uhub\-seeder to background in order to run it as a daemon.
.TP
.BI \^\-l " logfile"
Log messages to the given logfile (default: stderr)
.TP
.BI \^\-c " config"
Specify configuration file (default: /etc/uhub/uhub\-seeder.conf)
.TP
.BI \^\-C
Check configuration file and return. Will print either "OK" or "ERROR".
.TP
.BI \^\-p " pidfile"
Write the process id to the given file, and remove it on exit.
.TP
.BI \^\-h
Show the help message.
.TP
.BI \^\-V
Show the version number
.SH EXAMPLES
To run uhub\-seeder as a daemon, logging to a file and writing a pid file:
.TP
.B uhub\-seeder " -f -l /var/log/uhub/seeder.log -p /run/uhub/seeder.pid"
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/uhub/uhub\-seeder.conf
Default configuration file. It is a separate file from
.IR uhub.conf ;
the seeder does not read the hub's configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/uhub/seed/
Default seed cache directory. It holds the cached files, each named after its
verified TTH, and the SQLite database of cache metadata. The directory is
created with mode 0700.
